      "body": "## Motivation\n\nOn ROCm with the AITER MoE runner, `UnquantizedFusedMoEMethod.process_weights_after_loading` shuffles `w13_weight` and `w2_weight` with `aiter.ops.shuffle.shuffle_weight(..., (16, 16))` and stores the result with `copy_or_rebind_param`. `shuffle_weight` marks the tensor it returns with `is_shuffled = True`, but `copy_or_rebind_param` detaches it and copies the data into the existing `Parameter`, so the parameter that reaches `aiter.fused_moe` has no `is_shuffled` attribute.\n\n`aiter.fused_moe` reads `is_shuffled` to choose between the `preshuffle_on` and `preshuffle_off` CK 2-stage MoE modules and to accept tuned fMoE configs (it warns that tuned kernels expect preshuffled weights). As a result, unquantized BF16 MoE models always run the `preshuffle_off` path on weights that were shuffled, and tuned configs for these shapes cannot be applied.\n\nThis is the same issue that #47870 fixes for the compressed-tensors W8A8 FP8 MoE path, here in the unquantized path.\n\n## Modifications\n\nSet `is_shuffled = True` on `layer.w13_weight` and `layer.w2_weight` right after each `copy_or_rebind_param` call. Weight bytes, dtype and layout are unchanged; only the attribute that `aiter.fused_moe` checks is restored.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nMI350X (gfx950, 256 CUs), AITER `2bb5491`. One EP rank of a BF16 MoE layer: 512 experts (256 local via `expert_mask`), top-10, hidden 2560, expert intermediate 640, SiLU, fused gate/up, called through `aiter.fused_moe` exactly as `AiterRunnerCore` does. Output compared with a float32 PyTorch reference:\n\n| Tokens | Before: cosine / rel. error | After: cosine / rel. error |\n|---:|---|---|\n| 1 | 0.99999 / 0.0046 | 0.99999 / 0.0044 |\n| 16 | 0.999992 / 0.0040 | 0.999992 / 0.0040 |\n| 256 | 0.999993 / 0.0038 | 0.999993 / 0.0038 |\n| 4096 | 0.999992 / 0.0039 | 0.999992 / 0.0039 |\n\nEnd to end (TP2 + EP2 replica, greedy, this change plus tuned fMoE rows for the shape), answers and token log-probabilities stayed within run-to-run variation (mean absolute log-prob delta vs a fixed reference: 0.0145 / 0.0146 before, 0.0151 / 0.0167 after).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nSame layer, `aiter.fused_moe` per call (CUDA events, microseconds):\n\n| Tokens | Before | After |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | 140.2 | 106.3 |\n| 4 | 115.4 | 104.1 |\n| 16 | 159.1 | 146.1 |\n| 256 | 475.9 | 459.6 |\n| 1024 | 593.5 | 571.0 |\n| 4096 | 718.1 | 680.1 |\n| 16384 | 1859.2 | 1857.9 |\n\nWith the change the engine loads `module_moe_ck2stages_b16_b16_preshuffle_on_...` instead of `module_moe_ck2stages_b16_b16_preshuffle_off_...`, and tuned fMoE rows for the shape are picked up instead of the 2-stage default. End-to-end measurements were taken on SGLang `34c4ba1` with this change applied; the code path is unchanged on `main`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41703663575](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41703663575)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41703662756](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41703662756)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41703662869](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41703662869)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
