  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Confirming from the CT-FP8 side (#47870) — same bug class, and your perf numbers\r\nanswer a question I left open on mine.\r\n\r\nI measured accuracy identical with and without the tag (cos 0.999 either way) and\r\ncould not establish what the mislabel actually cost. Your 140 → 106 µs at 1 token\r\nand the tuned-config rejection is the answer: it is a throughput bug, not a\r\ncorrectness one.\r\n\r\nYour root cause is also a step subtler than ours — `shuffle_weight` sets the tag\r\nand `copy_or_rebind_param` drops it, whereas our path never set it. Worth a look\r\nat whether any other scheme routes a shuffled tensor through `copy_or_rebind_param`.\r\n\r\nBoth PRs are two/five lines and have the same nine reviewers; might be worth\r\nlanding them together.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-04T03:08:52Z",
